<title>USA: U.S. banks free reserves $618 mln Aug 28 two wks.</title>
<headline>U.S. banks free reserves $618 mln Aug 28 two wks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had free reserves of $618 million per day in the two weeks ended August 28, versus revised free reserves of $731 million in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $328 million versus $290 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
